{
  "__comment": "celastro's own dashboard. Every panel reads /api/metrics, scraped either by the chart's ServiceMonitor (monitoring.enabled) or by the scrape_config in deploy/README.md. Each panel's description says what its query is and what a bad value looks like; the metric names are the contract, and a release that renames one says so in the changelog. Import as it is: the only thing it asks for is a Prometheus datasource.",
  "title": "celastro",
  "uid": "celastro",
  "tags": [
    "celastro"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "label": "Prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "instance",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "label": "Node",
        "query": "label_values(celastro_attached_nodes, instance)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "sort": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Statements",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Statements a second",
      "description": "rate(celastro_statements_total[$__rate_interval]) per node. This counts statements the CONSOLE ran, so a node coordinating for the others shows more than the ones holding the shards; it is not a measure of the work each node did.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_statements_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Statement latency",
      "description": "The quantiles come from celastro_statement_seconds_bucket, whose widest bound under +Inf is 10 s: a p95 pinned at 10 means the 95th statement was SLOWER than the histogram can say, not that it took ten seconds. `max since start` is a gauge that never falls, so it is the worst statement this process has run, not a window.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(celastro_statement_seconds_bucket{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(celastro_statement_seconds_bucket{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "max(celastro_statement_seconds_max{instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "max since start"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Refused and failed",
      "description": "Refused is the guard: a missing or wrong token, a Host or Origin that did not pass. Failed is a statement the database ran and rejected, which includes every SQL error a user made, so it is normal for it to be non-zero where people type. A wire refusal is CELASTRO_WIRE_MAX_CONNECTIONS turning a peer away, and is not normal.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_requests_refused_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} refused"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_statements_failed_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} failed"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_wire_connections_refused_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} wire refused"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "The cluster",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Nodes attached",
      "description": "celastro_attached_nodes is how many OTHER nodes this one has verified since it started, so on a cluster of N every line should sit at N-1. A line that steps down and stays down is the alert CelastroNodeNotAttached; a line that steps down and back up is a pod that restarted.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "celastro_attached_nodes{instance=~\"$instance\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Catalog reconciliations",
      "description": "Definitions the sweep adopted from or dropped against a peer's catalog. A burst after a DDL or a rejoin is the mechanism working; a rate that never settles is two nodes disagreeing about the catalog and undoing each other.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_catalog_reconciled_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Backpressure",
      "description": "Writes that waited for compaction to catch up, and the time they spent waiting. The second line is the one that matters: at 1 a whole second of write time is being spent waiting every second, which is compaction losing to the write rate.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_backpressure_waits_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} waits/s"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_backpressure_seconds_sum{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} seconds waited/s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Shard reads and writes",
      "description": "Per shard, summed over the nodes holding it (a follower serves no reads, so the sum is the holder's). One shard far above the others is the hot shard SPLIT exists for.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 18,
        "y": 10,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (collection, shard) (rate(celastro_shard_reads_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{collection}}/{{shard}} reads"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum by (collection, shard) (rate(celastro_shard_writes_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{collection}}/{{shard}} writes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Storage",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Documents",
      "description": "sum by (collection) of celastro_documents, which each node reports for the shards IT holds -- so the sum is the collection, and it double-counts nothing as long as every node of the cluster is being scraped. A drop with no DELETE behind it means a node stopped being scraped.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (collection) (celastro_documents{instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{collection}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Segments",
      "description": "Sealed segments across the shards held here. Segments climbing while compactions stay flat is the maintenance thread falling behind, and the backpressure panel is where that starts to cost writes.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 19,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (collection) (celastro_segments{instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{collection}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Compactions",
      "description": "The second line is the fraction of wall-clock the maintenance thread spent compacting: near 1 it is saturated. A seal failure is a seal the maintenance thread will retry, and should be flat at zero; celastro_wal_bytes climbing beside it is the seal not landing.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 19,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_compactions_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} compactions/s"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_compaction_seconds_sum{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} seconds compacting/s"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "C",
          "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(celastro_seal_failures_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}} seal failures/s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "What pages someone",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Data keys kept",
      "description": "Above zero means a data-key rotation nobody finished: previous keys are still being kept so archived objects sealed under them open. `celastro key reseal` then `key retire` clears it. This is the alert CelastroDataKeyRingKept.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(celastro_data_key_ring_size{instance=~\"$instance\"})"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Certificate expires in",
      "description": "Days until the first node's certificate expires, from celastro_tls_certificate_expiry_seconds minus now. The series only exists where TLS is on, so an empty panel means plain TCP, not a certificate that never expires. Red inside 30 days, which is the alert CelastroCertificateExpiring.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 6,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "d",
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 30
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "min((celastro_tls_certificate_expiry_seconds{instance=~\"$instance\"} - time()) / 86400)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Shards nothing is reading",
      "description": "Shards that served no read in the last 15 minutes while the collection as a whole did. A shard is meant to take its share of the keyspace, so an idle one is usually a partition key that does not spread or a placement nobody re-balanced -- and occasionally a holder the map still names but no client reaches. Empty is the healthy state, and a cluster with no traffic at all makes it empty too.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 6
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "sum by (collection, shard) (rate(celastro_shard_reads_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[15m])) == 0 and on (collection) (sum by (collection) (rate(celastro_shard_reads_total{instance=~\"$instance\"}[15m])) > 0)"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true
            },
            "renameByName": {
              "Value": "reads/s"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
